{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And Elohim said to him, etc.</b> He agreed with him regarding his words, for he was not liable to death for what he had done, for it was with integrity of heart — but regarding cleanliness of hands He did not agree. Or perhaps, that even though he did not commit robbery, nevertheless the seizing of the kingship was through intermediacy; and even though it is not a robbery for which one would be liable, nevertheless it is not cleanliness of hands. Or it may be because in the words of HaShem there was no room for him to err, but Avimelekh was weighing all sides of the doubts — therefore there was no need to say to him ״and in cleanliness,״ etc." "And His saying <b>and I restrained you, etc.</b> — He intended to explain to him His intention, for what He had said to him, ״you are dead,״ etc., was not regarding what had already passed, but rather that if he would not return her and would draw near to her he would die. Therefore He warned him beforehand and restrained him by informing him that she was a married woman." "<b>from sinning against Me.</b> And the meaning of <b>against Me</b> is that even if He had not informed him and he had stumbled, the sin would not have made Avimelekh liable to death; nevertheless, with respect to Elohim there is a matter of strictness — both because of the nature of the act itself, that lying with another man's wife is immorality, and further because of Sarah and Abraham, for it is a disgrace to them, and they are the beloved friends of the Most High. Therefore He was precise in using the word <b>against Me.</b>" "And His saying <b>therefore,</b> etc., means: it is because the matter stands in this arrangement that I came to inform you, to restrain yourself from her. But besides this, He explained that if you had known she was a married woman and had taken her, I would have killed you — for the Holy One, blessed be He, judges the evil intent of the nations and counts it as deed. And according to their words, of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 52:13), who said that an angel pushed him off her, it is precisely indicated in the verse's saying <b>I did not let you touch her.</b>"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:35.455095680Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}